  "conclusions": [
    "First cancellation at tick 3653, simulation time 36.53s: operator direction 1 -> 0, FR lift -> abort_land, message Motion cancelled.",
    "The same Motion cancelled message lasts 82 control rows; at tick 3735 it changes to Landing before returning to wheel driving.",
    "Plain release/opposite keys produce Landing while side_active; watchdog alone retains the old message; a fresh poll after a long preceding tick restores held A.",
    "The recorded message selects the early-return branch: unfocused, X/R, stopped, or fallen. Fallen has a distinct message and Escape exits before logging; R press would create a new segment.",
    "The harness sends only A PRESS before waiting for side_success, then would send A RELEASE; no success occurred. Thus ordinary harness A release cannot explain this attempt.",
    "Focus loss is consistent with all observed evidence and the harness sequence. Exact focus event/source is not identifiable because received events and sent events were not persisted on failure.",
    "Failure reason is cancelled, not a support/liftoff/IK fault. The bridge kept side torque until landing completed at tick3831 and resumed legacy at3832."
  ],
